						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg9860#msg9860"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg9860#msg9860">Re: Rodcet Nife Allstars</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #29 on:</b> August 09, 2004, 08:48:18 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=991.msg9844#msg9844">Quote from: Delheru on August 08, 2004, 02:20:28 pm</a></div><div class="quote">Ranger:  uh... playskill wise I don&#039;t really think any rangers shone out. I know many of those mentioned here, and I haven&#039;t been impressed. Shar probably of those I know.<br /></div>I&#039;ve thought about people I would consider for this list as well, and you know, out of all the classes, I tend to have to agree with Delheru on this. <br /><br />Not because I think there are few skilled rangers, but because putting a real mark on a class that is so much a jack of all trades is hard to do. Add to the fact you have multiple ways to play the class, and none of them technically &quot;wrong&quot; it just comes down to opinions.<br /><br />As far as the rest of the classes, I know alot of good people, in all guilds, and to single it down to any single person, when I know/knew alot of very skilled players would mean I had to choose some of them over the others. And when you have a game like EQ with guilds that need to be a team and work together, singling a solitary person out of the crowd just diminishes the accomplishments of the rest as well.<br /><br />So I think the real all stars aughta be all those nuts still playing when the 6 year aniversary comes up.<br /><br /><span style="color: blue;">Silly Rangers can&#039;t even use quote tages correctly</span>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: August 09, 2004, 11:15:30 am by Kweil</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Guild Leader of <a href="http://www.fotguild.com" target="_blank">Fires of Time</a><br /><br /><span style="font-family: 2;">A little piece of paper with a picture drawn<br />&nbsp;floats on down the street till the wind is gone. <br />The memory now is like the picture was then, <br />When the paper&#039;s crumpled up, it can&#039;t be perfect again. </span>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
